---
# The GitHub App notification-controller's `github-status` Provider authenticates as, from the
# SOPS keys flux_github_app_id, flux_github_app_installation_id and flux_github_app_private_key.
# The App has its own rate limit, so a drained operator quota cannot stop a `flux/*` status post.
#
# A Secret of its own because the private key is a multi-line PEM block and both IDs are all
# digits: Flux strips every newline from a substituted value and types a standalone all-digit
# value as a number, so no `${...}` placeholder can carry any of the three. D3 ships this Secret
# as a SOPS-encrypted manifest instead. `render_sops_manifests` in defaults/main.yml names this
# file, so a placeholder render leaves it out. The IDs are quoted, never `| to_json`, because
# SOPS types an all-digit key int and to_json of an int emits bare digits, which the API server
# refuses as a stringData value. `to_json` writes the PEM as one double-quoted scalar, newlines
# escaped. notification-controller reads this Secret through the API on each event, so a
# rotation restarts nothing.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: flux-github-status
  namespace: {{ flux_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  githubAppID: "{{ flux_github_app_id }}"
  githubAppInstallationID: "{{ flux_github_app_installation_id }}"
  githubAppPrivateKey: {{ flux_github_app_private_key | to_json }}
